invariant: INV-17
file: sha3.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh keccak
reason: sha3_256 and sha3_512 no longer wipe the state they hash in, so
  the 25 lanes of the last permutation stay on the stack below the call
  after it returns. Keccak-f[1600] is a permutation, so the whole state
  gives back the state before it, as far back as the input, which under
  ML-KEM is a secret seed. Every digest is still right.
  bin/sha3_hw_equiv_test copies the stack below each kind of call and
  looks for any lane the call computed, and the script builds it with
  clang for arm64, the one object that holds sha3_hw.c, which compiles
  sha3.c once more. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    ct_wipe(lane, sizeof lane);
--- new
